{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Separately, Givaudan S.A. unveiled the Scentaurus M13, an AI-driven analytical instrument designed to quantify malodor molecules associated with pet and household odors. The product hit the market and generated a positive investor reaction, with Givaudan shares (ISIN CH0010645932) recording a notable uptick on June 27, 2026. Product Manager Dr. Marie Dupont described the Scentaurus platform as functioning like a "trained nose with a repeat button," integrating advanced pattern-recognition algorithms with Givaudan's extensive fragrance library to detect subtle variations in malodor intensity, particularly volatile sulfur compounds that human sensory panels may miss. CEO Gilles Andrier has emphasized that the data-driven nature of the instrument will differentiate Givaudan from competitors, especially as retailers increasingly demand verifiable product performance claims. The device is positioned to shorten formulation development cycles for cleaning and deodorizing products, though Givaudan acknowledges it is designed to complement, rather than replace, traditional sensory evaluation methods and complex analytical tools.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Also in the broader scientific landscape touching the M13 designation, Shirley, New York-based Creative Biolabs announced on April 30, 2026, upgrades to both its lambda and M13 phage display platforms, targeting advances in biotherapeutic research. The upgraded lambda phage genome library platform now accommodates large DNA inserts of up to 25 kilobases, supported by acoustic DNA shearing for controlled fragmentation, optimized size-selection workflows, and ultra-efficient in vitro packaging extracts achieving titers exceeding ten plaque-forming units per microgram of DNA. The enhanced M13 phage display platform supports ultra-diverse libraries reaching up to ten-to-the-tenth unique variants, with multiple display formats including pIII monovalent and pVIII multivalent configurations, alongside Trimer Codon }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 Technology}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  designed to eliminate stop codons and ensure uniform amino acid distribution. A Creative Biolabs spokesperson stated, "Phage based }{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ul\cf2 technologies}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  continue to shape the future of biotechnology. Our upgraded lambda and M13 platforms reflect our commitment to delivering advanced, customizable, and reliable solutions that help researchers achieve meaningful scientific breakthroughs."}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Turning to peer activity, General Catalyst finalized a landmark take-private transaction involving Janus Henderson Group Ltd. on June 30, 2026, alongside Trian Fund Management and Qatar Investment Authority. Under the terms of the deal, Janus Henderson's public shares were converted to cash at $52.00 per share and delisted from the New York Stock Exchange. Janus Henderson CEO Ali Dibadj expressed confidence in the transition, citing transformative opportunities in partnership with Trian and General Catalyst across investment solutions, }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 technology}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 , and talent development. The firm retains its operational presence in London and Denver under its current management structure. General Catalyst CEO Hemant Taneja stated the firm's commitment to enhancing Janus Henderson's technological capabilities and overall growth strategy. Trian's CEO Nelson Peltz noted the considerable progress Janus Henderson has made since Trian's initial investment in 2020. The transaction was backed by a broader investor group that includes MassMutual and Sun Hung Kai & Co.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 General Catalyst also participated in a $1.5 million seed funding round for Gurugram-based Omli, announced on June 17, 2026, alongside lead investor India Quotient. Founded in 2025 by Shivam Munshi and Siddhant Garg, Omli develops AI infrastructure specifically designed for children's speech and language development, addressing a recognized gap in commercial speech recognition systems that are predominantly trained on adult voice data. The company's flagship application, OmliKids, allows children aged three to ten to engage in voice-based conversations with an AI companion named Doro and has already recorded over 500,000 downloads on the Google Play Store since launch. To improve accuracy, Omli developed VedAnsh-v1, a proprietary speech-to-text and voice activity detection model tailored to children's speech patterns, including support for Indian accents and vernacular languages. Co-founder Siddhant Garg stated the company's ambition to achieve adult-grade accuracy in children's speech recognition. India Quotient's Madhukar characterized children as the largest consumer segment for which AI solutions remain largely undeveloped, underscoring investor confidence in the market opportunity.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 General Catalyst's Customer Value Fund led an $85 million growth round for Rylo, formerly known as Nagish, with participation from Canaan, Vertex Ventures, and Contour. The round pushes Rylo's total funding beyond $100 million. Headquartered in Tel Aviv and New York, Rylo develops AI-powered communication solutions for }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 Deaf}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  and hard-of-hearing individuals, offering real-time captioning for phone calls, speech-to-text conversion, text-to-speech capabilities, and in-person transcription. Following its acquisition of Sign.mt in 2025, Rylo launched Rylo Sign, enabling real-time translation between spoken and sign languages. Additional AI capabilities include speaker recognition, }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 sentiment}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2  analysis, and fraud detection. The newly raised capital will fund expansion of Rylo's engineering, product development, and commercial operations teams, as well as AI research, infrastructure development, and new workplace accessibility solutions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Lightspeed Venture Partners, through its Lightspeed Opportunity Fund, L.P., reported the divestiture of approximately $15.1 million in Netskope Inc. (NASDAQ: NTSK) Class A common stock across two transactions in June 2026, according to a recent SEC filing. On June 12, 2026, Lightspeed Opportunity Fund converted 1,650,000 shares of Class B common stock into Class A shares and subsequently sold 1,313,827 Class A shares at a weighted average price of $9.19 per share. On June 15, 2026, the fund sold an additional 336,173 Class A shares at a weighted average price of $9.00 per share, bringing total proceeds to $15,099,627. Following these transactions, Lightspeed Opportunity Fund holds no remaining Class A common stock in Netskope. Other Lightspeed entities collectively retained 62,843,207 shares of Class B common stock as of June 12, 2026, convertible into Class A shares on a one-for-one basis at the holder's option or automatically on September 19, 2035. The sales occurred as Netskope shares traded near $8.95, approximately 60% below their 52-week high and close to the 52-week low of $7.67. Netskope reported annual recurring revenue of $845 million, up 29% year-over-year, and total revenue of approximately $202 million, representing 28% year-over-year growth. Analyst price target adjustments followed the results, with TD Cowen reducing its target from $25 to $19 while maintaining a Buy rating, BMO Capital and RBC Capital lowering their targets to $13 with Outperform ratings, Piper Sandler reducing its target to $18, and Mizuho cutting its target to $13.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Lightspeed Venture Partners also appointed Rohit Kaul as its new marketing head, a move that comes as the firm prepares to raise its fifth India and Southeast Asia-focused fund, reportedly targeting approximately $500 million. Kaul previously served as Vice President of Marketing at Blume Ventures from February 2023, with additional experience at Sacra and HCL. His appointment follows the departure of former VP of Marketing and Communications Mansi Chugh after nearly four years in the role, and an earlier exit by Carina Chopra after three and a half years. Lightspeed has established a prominent position in India's startup ecosystem through investments in companies including OYO, Udaan, ShareChat, PhysicsWallah, and Pocket FM. Neither Kaul nor Lightspeed Venture Partners responded to queries prior to publication.}
